1. Host library (`libmimhid` shared, static, and runtime archives)
------------------------------------------------------------------

The host library (`libmimhid.so`, `libmimhid.dylib`, `mimhid.dll`,
`libmimhid.a`, `mimhid_static.lib`) is compiled solely from first-party MIT
source code in `src/`, `include/`, and `proto/`. It talks to the serial port
through operating-system primitives (`termios` on Linux and macOS, Win32 file
and SetupAPI calls on Windows) and links no third-party library dynamically or
statically. On Linux, the C++ runtime (`libstdc++` and `libgcc`) is linked
statically with `-Wl,--exclude-libs,ALL` under the GCC Runtime Library
Exception 3.1.

Every host binary archive (`*-shared`, `*-static`, and `*-runtime`) carries
`LICENSE`, this `NOTICE`, `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`, and `CHANGELOG.md` under
`share/doc/libmimhid/`, together with `build-metadata.json`. Every `*-shared`
and `*-static` archive has a matching SPDX 2.3 SBOM sidecar (`*.spdx.json`).

